    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d665">

                <pb facs="0637" n="625" sameAs="frus:frus1939v01/pg625"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">340.1115a/129: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the United
                        Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Kennedy</hi>)<anchor n="42"
                        xml:id="d665-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-10-05T16:00:00-05:00">October 5, 1939—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1164. The Government has decided that the repatriation problem has been solved to
                    the point where the use of the five specially diverted ships is no longer
                    necessary for that purpose. Two have already been released to their owners and
                    the <hi rendition="#italic">Iroquois, St. John</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Acadia</hi> will be released upon their return to the United States. The
                    regular passenger liners in the North Atlantic service will continue to make a
                    turn-around as quickly as possible and will be available for the carriage of
                    passengers to the United States from English, French and Irish ports.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d665-f1" n="42" type="source" xml:id="d665-f1-content">
                <p>The same telegram was sent on October 5 to the Ambassador in France as No. 1166,
                    and to the Minister in Ireland as No. 33.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
